<%# Favourite (add-to-scrapbook) button — THE one definition, rendered by every
    surface that has a favourite: the source/invert preview tiles, every
    candidate row and every finished-proof row. The preview popup does not
    re-implement it either: the layout renders this partial once into
    #csFavTemplate and aether.js CLONES it, so there is a single star, a single
    data-* contract and a single delegated handler (scrapFavourite) behind all
    of them — a change here cannot leave one surface behind.

    Locals: job_id, name, label (for the tooltip/aria), css_class, word
    (optional visible label; the popup's copy carries the word, the icon-only
    rows do not). The star is an inline SVG like the other row-action icons —
    text glyphs fall back inconsistently across the pixel/Inter font stack,
    which is exactly why the download/findings buttons use SVGs. %>
<button type="button" class="<%= local_assigns[:css_class].presence || "btn btn-icon fav-btn" %>"
        data-scrap-favourite data-scrap-job="<%= job_id %>" data-scrap-name="<%= name %>"
        title="Favourite <%= local_assigns[:label].presence || name %>"
        aria-label="Favourite <%= local_assigns[:label].presence || name %>">
  <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polygon points="12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2"></polygon></svg>
  <% if local_assigns[:word].present? %><span class="fav-word"><%= word %></span><% end %>
</button>
